From: juniorverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:10:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1p64100-microsoft-denali: drop the QMP PHY
 orientation switches

On the Surface Pro 11 both USB-C ports enumerate USB 2.0 devices, but the
SuperSpeed root ports stay in RxDetect (portsc Link=RxDetect, LEC=0 RLC=0
TLC=0), although the retimers are powered and configured with
conn_status 0x23/00/00 and the QMP combo PHYs are in USB3-only mode.
Every attach seen so far was reported as reverse by the ADSP.

Each port has two orientation switches in series: the PS8830 retimer
(orientation-switch on typec-mux@8) and, behind it, the QMP combo PHY
(orientation-switch in hamoa.dtsi). ps883x_sw_set() looks up the PHY switch
with typec_switch_get() and forwards every orientation change to it before
setting CONN_STATUS_0_ORIENTATION_REVERSED, so a reverse attach flips both
the retimer and the PHY lane mapping (SW_PORTSELECT_VAL).

Whether that double flip is correct depends on how the retimer host side
is wired, which the available data does not show: the X1E80100 CRD,
ThinkPad T14s and Surface Laptop 7 keep both switches. Delete the property
on both PHYs in the LCD board file so that they keep the normal lane
mapping and only the retimers flip. The PHYs stay registered through their
mode-switch property, so the USB3-only/DP mode selection from the retimer
is unchanged.

Normal-orientation attaches are unaffected. Reverse-orientation
DisplayPort alt mode places its lanes through the same PHY orientation and
may change; this is an experiment to be compared with the unmodified
behaviour.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts   | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
index a96f3595b..f88f6115f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1p64100-microsoft-denali.dts
@@ -188,3 +188,18 @@ ts_reset_n: ts-reset-n-state {
 		bias-disable;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The PS8830 retimers already carry the orientation switch of each port and,
+ * through ps883x_sw_set(), forward every orientation change to the QMP combo
+ * PHY behind them. Do not register the PHYs as orientation switches: they keep
+ * the fixed normal lane mapping and only the retimers flip. Experiment for
+ * reverse-orientation SuperSpeed; the PHYs stay registered as mode switches.
+ */
+&usb_1_ss0_qmpphy {
+	/delete-property/ orientation-switch;
+};
+
+&usb_1_ss1_qmpphy {
+	/delete-property/ orientation-switch;
+};
